Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add `insert_restored()` and replay a restored stack without
 `filter_next`

A saved behavior is loaded by inserting the current state together with
its `Memory` stack; `transition` then replays the stack as initial
pushes. Each replayed push still asked `Behavior::filter_next`, so a
saved stack whose current state is reachable from the state below it only
through states that have since stopped (`A -> B -> C`, saved as `[A]`
with `C` current) was rejected on load.

Skip the filter for initial pushes, since those states were admitted when
the stack was first built, and add `insert_restored()` as the public way
to insert a restored stack, as `Memory` is private. Test that `[A]` with
`C` current restores to `A` paused under `C`.
